---
import InfoPageLayout from '../layouts/InfoPageLayout.astro';
---
<InfoPageLayout
  eyebrow="Planned evaluation standard"
  title="Testing methodology"
  description="How future HydroRigor product evaluations will distinguish plans, observations, specifications, evidence, and conclusions."
  pathname="/testing-methodology/"
  relatedLinks={[
    { label: 'Reviews', href: '/reviews/' },
    { label: 'Comparisons', href: '/compare/' },
    { label: 'Editorial Policy', href: '/editorial-policy/' },
  ]}
>
  <aside class="rounded-xl border border-amber-measure/30 bg-mineral-sand p-5">
    <strong class="font-heading text-hydro-deep">Current reality</strong>
    <p class="mt-2">HydroRigor has not published real hands-on product testing in M03. This page defines a planned method; it is not evidence that a product has already been acquired or tested.</p>
  </aside>

  <h2>1. Define the use case first</h2>
  <p>A future evaluation should name the intended user, environment, job to be done, constraints, and criteria before a conclusion is formed. A product cannot be meaningfully described as “best” without a stated use case.</p>

  <h2>2. Label every evidence type</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Manufacturer specification:</strong> a published claim that has not automatically been verified by HydroRigor.</li>
    <li><strong>Third-party evidence:</strong> information from an identified external source.</li>
    <li><strong>HydroRigor observation:</strong> something directly observed under a disclosed test setup.</li>
    <li><strong>Editorial interpretation:</strong> a conclusion drawn from the available evidence and its limits.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Record a reproducible plan</h2>
  <p>Where practical, future testing should document the setup, duration, comparison baseline, instruments, criteria, anomalies, and limitations. The method should be proportionate to the claim being made.</p>

  <h2>4. Report limitations and updates</h2>
  <p>Results must not be generalized beyond the evidence. Supplied, loaned, or discounted products must be disclosed, and meaningful retests or product changes should be reflected in the update history.</p>
</InfoPageLayout>
